                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "78701251",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198837528031",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 39687,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 569,
                            "playtime_at_review": 2444,
                            "last_played": 1794270601
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played a lot of puzzle games before, but it's been a very long time since I've been this enthralled by one! There are so many interesting puzzle elements that are introduced completely organically, allowing you to understand them without the use of an explicit tutorial and, instead, through experimentation. New elements are presented even late into the game, which always made me excited to see what would lie in each new area. \nThe exploration is also fantastic, with secrets hidden in tricky to reach areas that give puzzles an extra layer of depth and make hunting around every nook and cranny feel properly rewarding. The amazing, outside-of-the-box solutions to some of the secrets were mind blowing and always felt amazing to figure out!\nMy only complaint might be the rather tight timing required on some puzzles can be difficult to wrestle with. For me, it was never completely unbearable, but it could get irritating. At best, it added an interesting challenge, but at worst, it turned some sections into a somewhat repetitive grind. Still, at the end of the day, the main challenge still feels overwhelmingly puzzle focused and mostly very tough, but fair. \nIf you're a hardcore completionist or challenge seeker, the vast array of puzzles and secrets will give you lots to have fun with and the user created challenges in the Level Pit will add even more! If you're a more casual puzzle fan, the game never puts an unbearable amount of pressure on you to do everything, and there are some tools to help you out with levels you might get stumped on, so you can stick to what you can manage and still have a rich and fun experience!\nAll in all, a wonderful game I'd recommend to both casual players and hardcore puzzle solvers!",
